OpenHub is a hard fork of OpenLogi, taken at commit b32ae087 on 2026-08-27.
The complete OpenLogi git history is preserved in this repository, so every
commit retains its original author. The two projects have different goals:
OpenLogi targets Logitech Options+ and productivity peripherals; OpenHub
targets Logitech G HUB and gaming peripherals — per-game profiles, macros with
repeat modes, and the HID++ features that gaming mice expose (0x8100 onboard
profiles, 0x8110 button spy).

OpenHub is an independent project. It is not endorsed by, affiliated with, or
supported by the OpenLogi project or its authors. Please do not report OpenHub
issues to the OpenLogi tracker.

